| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| "Push to web" / manual open claude.ai as first default | CDP via `team_dispatch(model=cdp/…)` per skill |
| Default binder/consult to a leftover `project_ask` recipe | Prefer `team_dispatch`; IF6 submit is CLI; warm paste is `cse_session(op=followup)` |
| Transport advice without loading CDP skill | `Use the claude-ai-cdp-navigation skill` first |
| Claim `workspaces://` unreachable on web; or cite `.cursor/skills/…` as the skill-delivery path | Prefer `cortex://` packaging for speed; Claude-slug engage or **inline** non-slugs for skills |
| Lead stages RAG then “merges” into deliverable when MCP `rag` is available (life or code) | Executing agent owns MCP `rag`; mapped URI is priming only |
| Aborting a CSE / dispatch because arc path changed | Poll **private bus lane** + paste into live converse; abort only with explicit operator auth (`session-abort-authorization_ulg.mdc`) |
| `active_work` empty ⇒ "CDP unreachable / arc dead" | Transport idle ≠ bus idle — operator-proxy commissions live on `agent_bus.request` thread |
| Skip `mcp`/`cdp_ask` (or any service) restart because it “would drop Cowork attach” | claude.ai is **resilient to all service restarts** — `drop(attach) ∧ ¬end(CSE)`; recover after `wait_healthy` (`restart-drain-discipline` § CSE vs service) |
| Hop or keep streaming so an open Cowork tab “stays alive” | Tab ⟂ session — PARK / idle tab is legal; hop is MCP-refresh or successor-confirmed continuity, never tab-keepalive (`decision:cse-tab-decoupled-from-session`) |
